        "original_id": "c1745973-9f5b-54e5-9441-b311af568f56",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mikael Åkerfeldt, Lee Ranaldo, Thurston Moore, Steven Wilson, Lunch, Martin Bisi\n- Bands/Projects: Opeth, Bloodbath, Steel, Storm Corrosion, Sonic Youth\n- Publications/Lists: Rolling Stone, Spin, Greatest Guitarists of All Time\n- Songs: “Death Valley '69”\n\nFacts:\n- Lee Ranaldo was born on February 3, 1956, and is an American musician, singer-songwriter, guitarist, writer, visual artist, and record producer.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt was born on 17 April 1974 and is a Swedish musician.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt is the lead vocalist, guitarist, and primary songwriter of Opeth.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt is the former vocalist of Bloodbath.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt was also guitarist for the one-off band Steel.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt is part of the collaboration Storm Corrosion with Steven Wilson.\n- Lee Ranaldo is best known as a co-founder of Sonic Youth.\n- In 1984, Thurston Moore and Lunch wrote and sang the song “Death Valley '69,” and Martin Bisi recorded it.\n- In 2004, Rolling Stone ranked Lee Ranaldo at number 33 on its Greatest Guitarists of All Time list.\n- In May 2012, Spin ranked Thurston Moore and Lee Ranaldo together at number 1 in a staff-selected top 100 list.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
